Z||000015||Fiero5||04-12-2001||09:02 AM||||I think the mystery is solved. Galen, here is an article that may explain the bizaar circumstances. It could have also happened in your neck of the woods?<P>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;<BR>The New York Times<P>TUESDAY, FEBRUARY 27, 2001 1:04 PM ET<P>The Bending Of Time. New Hampshire Town May Help Physics With Time Theory<P>By JAMES GLANZ<P>Boston, MA., Feb. 27 — New observations of the bending of Time in selected areas around the world have again resurfaced when a town in New Hampshire experienced time ripples early this morning around 3am. <BR>Subatomic Time particles do not appear to fit into the standard theories explaining the matter-antimatter equations and forces that shape the universe, scientists at Brookhaven National Laboratory reported today.<BR>Though the incredible Time event announced today in New Hampshire throw cherished Time flux ideas into question, space Time physicists have been waiting for such an excellent development for years because it opens a door into new worlds of Time theory.<P>Hanover New Hampshire is the most recent location in our hemisphere that has experienced a time bubble event*. It is a ripple that apparently displaces waves and waves of time energy throughout a given area. Hanover NH, a fairly good sized New England town and it's surrounding areas is the latest to experience this strange phenomenon. What little information that is being released so far is the unusual occurrence formed on the western side of New Hampshire in the Upper Connecticut River Valley area. The Connecticut river forms the border between Vermont and New Hampshire, and the residue from this time displacement event is apparently evident in these areas.<P>The Town of Hanover has a population of roughly 9,530 residents, and very few of them apparently have yet noticed or remarked about this time disturbance event. Dean of Dartmouth College, Jim Larimore stated in an interview this morning that his office was being very careful what they allowed out for information and comments on any incidents that the sciences department have discovered. Dartmouth College, which was established in 1769, is well known for it's sciences departments.<BR> The rural sections of Town are Hanover Center and Etna. It is unclear at this time how far out this time bubble may have stretched. The elevation in this area is approximately 603 feet, and the time ripple may have reached out on a further path than is being discussed at this time.<P>Located near Interstates 89 and 91, Hanover is 2 hours from Boston, 3 hours from Montreal, and 5 hours from New York City. The center of the ripple is believed to have started near the most populated area of Town which is near the river and the College.<P>The impact of such an occurrence is yet to be calculated. Local officials are now just being informed of the event by special representatives were flown in for this unusual occurrence and are working with faculty from the local college. <P>The college sits within the other local schools that are made up within the Dresden School District. This district  includes the Richmond Middle School, the Hanover High School, the Ray School in Hanover and the Marion Cross School in Norwich and of course Dartmouth College. There has been no word yet if any of the schools or the college were effected by the time ripple.<P>David Kotz, a Dartmouth College faculty member in the sciences department was quoted in the Boston Herald early this morning that his department has tracked the possible wake signature of the time ripple. Located in the Sudikoff Laboratory which is where the computer Science lab is housed, he and another science faculty member have charted the aftermath of the apparent time wake. "Clifford Stein and myself have calculated the probable path of the time dispersement in Hanover and the surrounding valley."<BR>There are six research laboratories and a machine room at the sciences area of the college, which include equipment dedicated to specific research projects. It is believed that as much as 5 of the 6 laboratories have been refocused on this latest time phenomenon.<P>Dr. Gerald Gabrielse, a professor and chairman of the physics department at Harvard University, called the latest Time ripples in New Hampshire as "tremendously exciting" because of the possibility of the current and  accepted Time theory's had been breached. But they said the measurements being conducted by the science department at Dartmouth had so far determined with 99 percent probability that this would destroy those theory's. They said they were already gathering and analyzing more data that could eliminate the one chance in a hundred that this latest event was a fluke.<P>"It could lead to a whole deeper understanding of how reality and time is put together," Dr. Gabrielse said. Among the leading possible reasons for the difference, physicists said, would be the existence of previously undetected Eactons, or time waves that ripple throughout the galaxy with strange properties affecting the way the muons work in the space time continuum, or processed, in the magnetic field causing time displacement.<P>Physicists have long known that the Eacton rate is affected by the properties of space itself. Under the laws of quantum mechanics, which rule the subatomic realm, apparently empty space is actually a sea of what scientists call "virtual time particles" that briefly appear and disappear and can also interact with muons.<P>"This latest event in New Hampshire could change the way we live and think about life", Dr. Gabrielse said. "Only Time will tell."||||reg||1
Z||000016||Formula88||04-12-2001||09:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>Why do all the moons of all the planets have names except ours?<P>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-12-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Unless I'm mistaken, our moon's name is Luna.  The sun's name is Sol and the earth is referred to either as Earth or Terra, depending on your sources.  If someone with more Astronomy sources than my dusty memory care to correct me, feel free.||||reg||3
